  "description": "SUB-700 G CARBON FRAME\n\nBuilt using Toray T1100G carbon and HCIM (Hollow Core Internal Molding) technology, the Ultralight frame weighs under 700 g — 11% lighter than the previous generation — while maintaining exceptional torsional and lateral stiffness.\n\n+12% AERODYNAMIC EFFICIENCY*\n\nThe Ultralight inherits the Aerolight’s aerodynamic DNA, with Kammtail tube profiles, an integrated aero seatpost and optimised transitions that reduce drag.\n\nIts aerodynamic performance has been developed and validated through CFD simulations in collaboration with the University of the Basque Country (EHU).\n\n*Requires 12% less power at 60 km/h than the previous generation. CFD study conducted by EHU.\n\nRACE GEOMETRY BUILT FOR COMPETITION\n\nA 74° seat tube angle and compact 405 mm chainstays promote efficient pedalling and deliver quicker acceleration, with a direct, responsive ride feel.\n\nINTEGRATED AERO FORK\n\nDesigned to reduce turbulence around the front wheel and optimise airflow. Compatible with tyres up to 35 mm(*).\n\n*Guaranteed clearance for tyres up to 32 mm. Compatible with most 35 mm tyres, depending on their actual dimensions.\n\nINTEGRATED CARBON COCKPIT\n\nAll models feature the Vision Metron Evo S, an integrated carbon handlebar designed by Vision to maximise aerodynamics, stiffness and comfort. Its wing-shaped profile optimises airflow, while its 10° forward angle promotes a more natural riding position.\n\nINTEGRATED AERO SEATPOST\n\nThe Ultralight’s aero seatpost features an aerodynamic profile and a fully concealed seatpost clamp, reducing drag while creating a cleaner, more integrated look.\n\nLIGHTWEIGHT THRU-AXLES & UDH\n\nMachined thru-axles reduce weight and deliver a cleaner finish. The dropout is SRAM UDH-compatible, making replacement straightforward and ensuring compatibility with the SRAM ecosystem.",
